## Summary

Hyperactivity is the coordination layer of computation, knowledge and credit. In it every computation is identified by its content and carries its proof, every work is credited through what it is built from and who carried it, anything derived once is never paid for again, and credit is conserved, so it allocates what money allocated.

The world spends about $22 trillion a year on flows that are information work: about $6.37 trillion on information technology, about $5.8 trillion on education, about $9 trillion on health, about $1.34 trillion on advertising. Most of that is rent: on recomputation, on intermediation, on lock-in, on error and on ignorance. Each rent exists because of a decision made around 1970, when storage was made of meaningless bytes, machines were made endpoints of other machines, and screens were divided into the walled worlds of separate programs. Hyperactivity is the form of computing those decisions foreclosed: data as a value with its type, identity by content, machines meeting as peers that check what they receive, and the person's own things shown through views the person owns.

The mathematics is done and machine-checked. Observation fibers say exactly what a reading warrants and when a participant is safe to act. Univalence makes an equivalence an identity, so a change of representation carries every operation and every proof across at once. A language is a value, so C, C++, Rust, OCaml, Python and x86 are presentations inside one host. Specialization keeps its proof, so the fastest code is also proven code. A maintained result carries the proof that it is the result, and a cached evaluation carries the certificate of everything it read, so reuse is a theorem. Credit is conserved under allocation and delivery with no global scheduler. Definitions are exchanged by content with their proofs, with no global namespace and no canonical state.

Out of that mathematics come the economics. A computation run n times costs n·c when each run starts from nothing, and c plus n lookups when its result is held with its proof, so the share of computation that is already derived goes to 1 and its price goes to 0. Money's value is 0 exactly where money is not the allocator of anything wanted. Profit in trading measures collective ignorance, and a system that dispels it at machine speed makes prices converge on what is true. What Hayek said prices had to carry, because no planner could hold it, becomes directly available with its evidence to every participant, so prices stop being the main way an economy coordinates.

In 2026 the largest technology companies will spend about $725 billion on capital, and total compute capex is about $1.04 trillion, most of it to run language models. A language model is a bandaid on poor information management. It is the one bridge that reads meaningless bytes and guesses what they mean, and each of its tasks (search, summarization, code, answers) is a guess standing in for a missing type, a missing equality or a missing proof. The exact object it approximates (an index of every repeated sequence of every length, with what followed each) fits in linear space. Meaning derived from the record says exactly where a text-only model's meaning is determinate and where it is not. When the information is managed, the bandaid is worth nothing. The bubble is the price of the bandaid, and the launch that removes its value is Avik's.

The fronts run in parallel: the trading firm built as one program; music without a middle; chemistry with correct identity for medicine; education by curriculum inversion; the language and its lineage; intelligence that is exact; neural co-processing; the trust market; Tesla's world system; and the people who carry it. Each removes a rent large enough to reach a share of ten trillion on its own.

The value is realized the way the work says value is realized. Alpha is exposure: presenting present information the market lacks, and being paid for the activity the exposure releases. Forcing the outcome: investing in a set of initiatives, then handing them the construction they need to work perfectly. The firm built as one program concentrates its market. Conserved credit flows to sources, and the work is at the root.

Ten trillion dollars is the present value of $500 billion a year at a 5% discount rate: 2.2% of the information-work flows, 7.9% of IT spending alone. A thousand sequences of choices, each reaching the outcome with probability 1%, all fail together with probability 0.00004. They share no point of failure, because the one thing they share is mathematics already checked, and they share every success, because every result one of them derives enters the graph for the rest.

