## 40. Exposure

Alpha is exposure: present the present information to the market and be paid for the activity the exposure releases in the economy (Q5). The mature market looks like investigative research: never predicting a price, but asking what information the current price reflects, and whether it already reflects the exposure of this information. The quant operates over a market ignorant of the true value of things and is tasked with exposing it. Human ignorance of underlying value is fundamental to the problem definition; what humans have yet to discover is the economic value awaiting (Q7.4).

The information here is the repricing. The market prices LLM-centric scale as though the bandaid were the cure. It prices the middle (platforms, stores, labels, ad networks) as though the walls of 1970 were permanent. It prices the dollar as the allocator of things it will stop allocating. Each price reflects an ignorance of what the work establishes. Holding that information first, and positioning on it before it is exposed (short what reprices down, long what reprices up), is the first capture. Then the exposure itself, the launch, releases the activity that moves the prices. Avik's statement: "I'm in control of the situation and I'm forcing the reality."

The positions are sized by the size of the repricings: the compute capex built on the bandaid, the market value of the companies whose revenue is the middle, and the assets that gain when the middle goes.


### The dollar as a metric of loss

Quantitative research is research into the quantitative loss of an information system (Q6). A price compresses everything the market knows about a thing into one number, and the compression loses the fundamentals: the interaction chains that make the thing valuable, the evidence for each, and what is not yet known. The dollar measures that loss. Economics that models only the number erases what the number lost.

So the exposure is not only a trade on prices. It is the replacement of the number by what it compressed. When the knowledge prices carry is directly available with its evidence (S4), the number stops being the main way an economy coordinates, and a scalar financial system becomes one view among many over a richer account. The success of the work is indivisible from that end (Q6.2). The positions profit from the transition; the transition is the point.

