# Part Nine. Precedent, why now, lineage and credit

## Precedent

Seventeen companies were worth over a trillion dollars at points in 2026, sixteen in the latest count, together more than $35 trillion. In 2018 there was one. The tier is not a fantasy; it is a club with a membership list. Two of the people best placed to judge expect a billion-dollar company run by one person. And the middle that the work removes is priced every day in the market value of the companies that hold it.

What has no precedent is the layer beneath all of them: one construction under computation, knowledge and credit. That is why the figure is ten trillion and not one.


## Why now

Four things are true at once in November 2026, and none was true five years ago.

**The mathematics is done.** Computational cubical type theory runs univalence as computation; the paper builds identity, transport, languages as values, specialization with paths, native execution with a theorem, maintained results, dependency certificates and conserved credit on it, and the constructions check. The archive behind it is more than 100,000 lines of machine-checked mathematics.

**One person can build it.** Agents working through tooling that addresses their failure modes do the engineering at machine throughput, so one person who holds the whole design builds the whole system. For a decade the gap was materializing value in information systems, because coding was physical suffering; that gap is nearly closed. The heads of the two leading AI labs expect a billion-dollar company run by one person for exactly this reason.

**The bubble is at its peak.** The largest companies are spending a trillion dollars a year on the bandaid, more than half of revenue at one of them, on the expectation that it returns. The gap between that price and what is true is at its widest.

**The cost structure has inverted.** Storage and computation are nearly free and on every device; what is scarce is knowing what a thing is. The form of computing that answers that question by the thing itself is the form that matches what things now cost.

Hyperactivity is inevitable whenever humans progress. Now is when it is first.

